**Heavy-slot mechanism (the project's, as B566, B577 and B580 used it).** Heavy = `dotnet build`, `dotnet test` (also `--list-tests`), `npm ci`, `npm run lint`, `tsc -b`, `vitest run`, `npm run build`, a mutant matrix, the differential, the CI line. Take ONE slot atomically with full paths: `mkdir` `.tools/heavy-slot-1`, else `-2`, else `-3` under the project root (`2>/dev/null ||` chain); write `B581 <time from date> <label>` into its `holder` file; read every other holder first and NEVER touch, move or remove another seat's holder (a slot with no holder file is reported, not taken over by force: `mkdir` fails on it, take another); one slot, one job at a time. **Release by MOVE** of your own slot into `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-24_B581_<slot>_<label>/`, never `rm`; before your last line `ls .tools | /usr/bin/grep heavy-slot` shows no holder naming B581. **Load:** start a heavy job only while load1 < 7 at two reads 4 s apart, recorded beside the result (`uptime` refreshes about every 5 s: the reads are not independent; say so); re-read before EACH heavy job inside the slot; if >= 7 poll every 30 s and do the light work meanwhile (Checks 1, 7, 8, 9, the CI reads, the greps of Check 2). **A MOVING heartbeat** (a counter plus the time from `date`) goes to `.tools/b581/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. **Never wait with `pgrep -f <pattern>` from a shell whose own argv holds the pattern** (it matches itself and never ends): wait on a recorded pid (`kill -0`) or a done-marker file your job writes last. **Every command gets its input or none** (a stdin-reading command with no input hung 68 minutes in an earlier drafter: give it a file, a here-string or `/dev/null`). **Never leave a background job running when you finish.**
**Locks:** the shared `.tools/.git-lock` wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY (your explicit-refspec `fetch` into your own clone): `mkdir` to take, `rmdir` at once to release; if it exists, poll 20 s, never break it.
**NuGet, npm and CLI homes are SEAT-LOCAL** under `.tools/b581/`: `DOTNET_CLI_HOME`, `NUGET_PACKAGES`, `NUGET_HTTP_CACHE_PATH`, `NUGET_PLUGINS_CACHE_PATH`, `npm_config_cache=.tools/b581/npm-cache` set BEFORE the first restore, proven from each worktree's `obj/project.assets.json` `packageFolders` (only `.tools/b581/nuget/packages`; this is round 1's B566-2 and a seat that reads a neighbour's NuGet home has made that finding again); `npm ci` only inside YOUR worktrees' `web/`, never in `2_Project_Files/web`. SDK = project-local `.tools/dotnet/dotnet`; build with `-nodeReuse:false -p:UseSharedCompilation=false`, `DOTNET_CLI_USE_MSBUILD_SERVER=0`, `MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1`. **Node:** the project's `.tools/` holds no node; the box has `/opt/homebrew/bin/node` (record `node --version`, `npm --version`; the gate before this one and the builder ran 26.8.1 and got CI's counts; CI runs node 24: "node 24 (CI) NOT RUN" unless you have one without opening another seat's tree). List `~/.nuget`, `~/.dotnet` and `~/.npm` before and after: unchanged except what you name.

## CHECKS (each: FAIL first, clock from `date`, YOUR instrument, a control that can fail)
**Instrument setup.** Own clone `.tools/b581/repo` (`git clone --shared` of `2_Project_Files`, `core.sshCommand` as the project sets it, every `pushurl` = `DISABLED-no-push`, proven by `remote -v`); fetch explicit refspecs under your lock, no prune: `+refs/heads/b561/mps-proposal-combined-usage-rate:refs/remotes/origin/b561/mps-proposal-combined-usage-rate`, `+refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/origin/main`, `+refs/pull/105/merge:refs/remotes/origin/pr/105-merge`, and the heads of #104 and #106 for Check 8 (`git cat-file -t <sha>` first: the local clone may be stale; the objects `4db8661d`, `ce6aedfb`, `459db8b8` must read `commit`). Detached worktrees from YOUR clone as under PARTITION. Never `pkill`, `killall` or a kill by name; stop only your own PIDs, proved by cwd or argv (`b581` in the line); prove ports free after.

**1. Delta, hygiene (C1).** FAIL: a path beyond the four; a commit count other than 3 (`rev-list --left-right --count 4db8661d...ce6aedfb` = `0 3`; `merge-base --is-ancestor` rc 0; each commit one parent, the chain `4db8661`, `1d6ec5d`, `3a9972b`, `ce6aedf`; control: a planted extra path is flagged); numstat other than `2 3` (`sections.ts`), `18 0`, `26 0`, `1 1` (sum +47 -4); **removed lines: print every `-` line your parser finds in `git diff -U0 4db8661d ce6aedfb` over the range AND per commit. Expected exactly 4: the `sections.ts` constant line and its two comment lines, and `DealUsageColourRowTests.cs:290` (`>= 20` to `>= 100`, the rest of the line byte-equal: prove it by replacing `100` with `20` in the head's line and comparing it with the base line). Any other removed or changed line, in particular in `dealPair.test.tsx` or `DealUsageCombinedPair.cs`, is a Blocker** (control: a planted removed line counts 5). Rebuild each of the two pure-addition test files' base from the head by deleting the added line ranges named in the `-U0` hunk headers and compare its sha256 with the base blob (control: delete one extra line, hashes differ). **Fence: `git diff 4db8661d ce6aedfb -- src docs .github web/src/api web/e2e web/src/proposal/OnePager.tsx web/src/proposal/ProposalDocument.tsx web/src/proposal/fixtures web/src/proposal/model.ts '*.css' '*.csproj' Directory.Build.props global.json package.json package-lock.json` is 0 bytes** (control: the same fence over `a5b4bbb5..4db8661d` is non-empty). Neighbours byte-equal base-to-head by blob (`rev-parse <sha>:<path>`; control: two different blobs differ): `src/MpsCalc.Api/Quotes/Proposal.cs`, `src/MpsCalc.Api/Contracts/Dtos.cs`, `docs/api/openapi.json`, `web/src/api/generated/schema.ts`, `tests/MpsCalc.Api.Tests/B103DealUsageCountedLineTests.cs`, `tests/MpsCalc.Api.Tests/B103DealUsageProposalTests.cs`. **Tree check:** `rev-parse ce6aedfb^{tree}` against `rev-parse refs/pull/105/merge^{tree}` (equal means the CI merge tree is byte-equal to the head tree because the merge ref was computed before main moved: say which, and say that CI therefore did NOT build the combination with `459db8b8`). Each commit carries the `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` trailer. Hygiene over the 47 added lines AND all three commit messages (each count printed, each with a planted-line control): `Skip =`, `.skip(`, `.only(`, `todo`, `#if`, `Trait`, `Thread.Sleep`, `Task.Delay`, `DateTime.Now`/`UtcNow`, `new Random(`, `Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable`, a URL: 0; non-ASCII bytes 0 (`LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c -E '^\+.*[^ -~]'`; control: a planted raw byte counts 1); no person's name (read from the config, never printed), no ticket key (`MPSCALC-n`), no `B5nn`, no gate finding id (`B566-n`), no mutant id (`M3a`, `G1`, `W-M1` and the like), no card id and no percent figure in an added line or a message (controls: planted lines); no `Skip`, `Trait` or environment gate on the new rows. **Names:** `dotnet test --list-tests` for the Api project at `-prev` and `-head` (parse method and case lines by program) and `vitest run --reporter=json` for web (file, describe and test names): lost 0; added exactly the builder's 6 Api names (the Theory `CombinedPair_a_deal_colour_total_of_a_page_or_less_still_prints_the_colour_row`, 3 cases x 2 hosts) and 1 web name (the new `it` in `dealPair.test.tsx`); Engine and Import lists equal (control: a dropped name reports lost 1, a renamed one lost 1 and added 1). **Decimals:** list every numeric literal in the added lines by program (control: a planted `1234.56m` is listed); all must be invented: the Theory's `100`, `50`, `1` (hundredths of a page), the divisor `100m`, the added line's quantity `1`, the mono pages `50`, the line number `9`; any other literal is a finding. A new file NAME carrying a brief number: none expected (no file is created).

**2. THE RENDERED CELL (C2; must-check 3). The words are the product owner's; the gate reads, it does not judge wording.** FAIL: the device-class cell of a deal-wide usage row reads anything other than exactly `All device classes` in EITHER document; the constant reaches a place the comment does not name; a section-rate row prints the words; the summary labels gain a bracket or the words. State the FAIL before the run; write your predictions into STATUS BEFORE any render (expected: the cell reads `All device classes` in the one-pager's `table.pd-one-rates` and in the full proposal's usage table (head cell text `Usage component`), the constant reaches NOTHING else, the summary labels read `Monochrome office prints` / `Colour office prints`). **(a) The DOM text, both documents, locally.** In `-mut` (head) write a scratch vitest file with a distinct name under `web/src/proposal/` (never committed; ASCII only) that renders `<OnePager proposal=...>` and `<ProposalDocument proposal=...>` (the harness the committed `dealPair.test.tsx` uses: `@testing-library/react`, jsdom) for: the five-class deal fixture `fiveClassDealProposal()`, a one-class deal, a mono-only deal rate, a colour-only deal rate, a deal row whose class KEY is absent (the `noClassKey` shape), the section-rate fixture `s4Proposal()`, and a proposal with no usage rows; write one TSV row per `td`/`th` of every table (document, table heading or class, row index, cell index, `textContent`, and the code points of the cell text as a list) to `.tools/b581/logs/`. **The device-class cell of each deal-wide row must read exactly `All device classes`** (18 code points, all ASCII 32-122, no NBSP, no zero-width, no trailing space; control: your own scratch rendering of a cell holding `All device classes ` with a trailing space reads "not exact"). Read the DOM text, do not take `T.DEAL_WIDE_CLASS_CELL` as the oracle. Row counts: print rows in each document (the deal pair is 2 rows; the "and N more rates" line must not appear for the deal; the section-rate fixture keeps its rows). **(b) Where the constant reaches (tracer).** In `-mut` set the constant to a tracer value `ZZ581TRACER` and re-render all the fixtures: count the tracer by table and by cell column in both documents; expected: only the device-class column of the one-pager's rates table and of the full proposal's usage table, only for deal-wide rows, 0 in the summary table, 0 in the stream labels and cards, 0 in the Media row, 0 for the section-rate fixture. Then the same tracer in `-mutprev` (`4db8661d`, constant `''` replaced by the tracer): **was the constant rendered in the summary table at `4db8661d`? (expected no: `rateSummaryLabel` never calls `classLabel` for a null class) and is it now? (expected no)** Say whether the old comment's "summary table" claim was real; it is gone from the head's comment. Restore both trees byte-equal (sha256 before/after, `git diff --quiet` rc 0). **(c) Grep, every use** (`git grep -n -F DEAL_WIDE_CLASS_CELL` at the head over `web docs src tests`, control `zzz-no-such-string-7f3a` reads 0): exactly the 10 hits listed under THE SUBJECT; map each `classLabel` caller (`OnePager.tsx:282, :318, :331`, `ProposalDocument.tsx:326, :424, :425`) to its argument's type in `schema.ts` and `model.ts` and say which can receive null (expected: only `:318` and `:424`; the stream callers' `deviceClass` is the non-null union, so they cannot print the words; if one CAN be null, render it with a null and report what it prints: a Major if it prints the words where the ruling does not name them). Also `git grep -n -i -F 'all device classes'` at the head over `web docs src tests` (expected: the constant, the new `it`'s local `words`, the new `it`'s title; print them) and the docs frame for any text that calls the cell "empty" or blank (the builder's grep: 0; control `zzz-no-such-string-7f3a` 0). **(d) The literal census (the words rule), by program** (your own tokenizer, TS string literals and JSX text, comments skipped; control: a planted literal reads one more) over the web files of the delta at `4db8661d` and the head: `sections.ts` head-only literals = exactly 1 (`All device classes`) and base-only = exactly 1 (the empty string); `dealPair.test.tsx` head-only = the new row's literals (`''` x2 for the `?? ''` defaults, `'td, th'`, the test title, `'All device classes'`, `'Monochrome office prints'` x2, `'Colour office prints'` x2 RELAYED), base-only 0; C# literals added in `DealUsageCombinedPair.cs`: the Theory's strings only (`colourPagesPerDeviceMonth`, `bomLines`, `monthlyColourPages`, `lfp` and two assertion messages RELAYED); `DealUsageColourRowTests.cs` head-only 0 and base-only 0. **Any other changed or added user-facing string is a Blocker.** **(e) Optional bridge (PROBED, only if the heavy-slot budget allows; else NOT TESTED):** a scratch Api test in `-mut` serialises the proposal JSON of a real deal-usage quote (the Theory's draft shape, the Api test host in process, no port) to a file; a scratch web test parses that file and renders both documents: the cell reads `All device classes` for the server's own `deviceClass: null` rows. **(f) Fit:** the longer cell (18 characters against 12 at most) cannot be seen in jsdom; read `proposal.css:59-60`, `one-pager.css` and the print rules for any fixed width or `nowrap` on `.pd-one-rates` / the usage table cell and say what you read; **the fit in a real browser and in print is NOT TESTED BY DESIGN** (a Note for the product owner's eye, not a finding).

**3. The new rows against the source: red first where they can be, green at the head, the floor (C3; must-checks 1, 2 and 4).** Write your predictions into STATUS BEFORE any run. (a) **The new web `it`** (`dealPair.test.tsx`, the `it` whose title begins "the deal-wide class cell reads All device classes"): in `-prev` (`4db8661d`, constant `''`) copy ONLY the head's `dealPair.test.tsx` as an untracked change; `vitest run src/proposal/dealPair.test.tsx` predicted 7 ran, **1 red** (the new row, at its one-pager expectation, `expected [ '', '' ] to deeply equal [ 'All device classes', 'All device classes' ]`), 6 green; print the failing text and rc; restore byte-equal. At the head: 7 of 7 green. (b) **The Theory** (`CombinedPair_a_deal_colour_total_of_a_page_or_less_still_prints_the_colour_row`, 3 cases): read it whole with its helpers (`DealUsageDraft`, `PlotterLine`, `DealRows`, `Dec`, `DealMonoRow`, `DealColourRow`, which this delta does not edit): it removes the colour estimate from every existing bom line and adds one counted plotter line in `lfp` (quantity 1, 50 mono pages, the colour total), asserts FIRST that the engine's `monthlyColourPages` equals the total exactly and THEN that the rows are exactly mono then colour, class null, no label. Predicted: GREEN at `-prev` and at the head, on both hosts (it is a test-strength fix: **there is no red-at-base for it, say so**; its proof is the mutants of Check 4); confirm the engine and the API accept the three totals (`monthlyColourPages` reads 1, 0.5, 0.01 in the assertion; print the three values); a refusal of a fractional estimate would be a finding against the builder's premise. Run filter `CombinedPair` at the head: 30 ran RELAYED (24 existing + 6 new). **A weak-row control (cw-weak):** a scratch copy of the Theory with its second assertion (the rows) dropped, plus mutant M3a, reports 1 unkilled (the matrix can see a weak row); and a copy with only the rows assertion, plus a mutant that moves `monthlyColourPages` (say the page sum scaled by 2), shows the first assertion fires. (c) **The floor (B566-6):** at the head print the counter yourself on BOTH hosts with a scratch print in `-mut` (seed 20261023, 600 cases: `mixedDeals`, `colourRowsPrinted`, `colourRowsDropped`, `monoRowsPrinted`; RELAYED 141 / 314 / 125 / 436; restored byte-equal, `git diff --quiet` rc 0); `>= 100` must be green at your value on both hosts and you say the margin (value minus 100); read `:282` and say what the counter counts now against main's `:296` (the line is restored as a number; the counter's meaning is per deal, not per class). The closure test is in Check 4 (G1). (d) **Per commit** at `-prev`: overlay commit 1 (the two web files), then commit 2, then commit 3: each stage builds (web `tsc -b`, `vitest`; .NET build 0 warnings) and the stage's tests are green. (e) **Census:** the Theory has no `Skip`, `Trait`, sleep, zone, culture or order dependence (read it; the repeats are in Check 6).

**4. Mutants, B566-1 and B566-6 (C4; must-checks 1 and 2).** Whole project of the file the mutant lives in, in `-mut` at the head, one at a time, rebuilt from the text of this brief and the sources (NOT from the builder's list). For each: anchor count printed (= 1), sha256 before/during/after, the tamper read back, build rc (a non-building mutant is BROKEN, not killed), the count that ran (> 0), red rows BY NAME split into NEW rows (the Theory's 6 names, the web `it`, the floor line) and OLD rows, byte-equal restore, `git diff --quiet` rc 0 after each, never committed. **Write the per-mutant predictions before the matrix.** **Server (anchor `> 0m;` in `src/MpsCalc.Api/Quotes/Proposal.cs` at `:519`, the text `countedLines.Sum(l => l.Quantity * (l.ColourPagesPerDeviceMonth ?? 0m)) > 0m;`; count it yourself), Api filter `CombinedPair|DealUsage|B103_214|Proposal|Showcase|A2_|section_rate` (227 RELAYED = 221 + 6) first, then the WHOLE Api project once for each survivor and once for `> 1m` (round 1's survivor, 2,240 ran then):** M3a `> 1m`, M3b `>= 1m`, M3c `> 0.5m`, M3d `> 0.01m`, M3e `> 0.005m`, M3f `>= 0.01m`, M3g `> 0.001m`, D10 `>= 0m`, D3 (the colour row printed without the pages test: drop the clause), M1 (`Count > 0` to `Count > 1` at the mono guard), M4 (the predicate over every line, `p.Lines`). **Web (anchor `'All device classes'` at `sections.ts:384`, `return T.DEAL_WIDE_CLASS_CELL;` at `OnePager.tsx:96` and `ProposalDocument.tsx:30`; `vitest run src/proposal` first (179 RELAYED), then the whole web suite for any survivor):** W1 constant to `''`, W2 `'All classes'`, W3 `'All device class'` (singular), W4 `'all device classes'` (lower case a), W5 `'All device classes '` (trailing space), W6 OnePager's `classLabel` null branch returns `''`, W7 ProposalDocument's returns `''`, W8 `rateSummaryLabel` keeps a bracket for a null class, W9 section rows print the constant (one per host file), W10 the null branch returns the raw `deviceClass`/`undefined`-string. **Floor