t` (section-rate cells); W3, W4, W5 (near-miss spellings) die on the new `it` because its literal is typed in the test, not read from `T`; a survivor among them is a Major.** **Tables:** mutant, anchor count, sha256 before/mutated/after, ran, red total, red in NEW rows by name, red in OLD rows by name, restore proof; and the **row-kill table**: for each new row (the 6 Theory names, the web `it`, the floor line) the mutants that turn it red. Property: every new row is killed by at least one mutant. Report the builder's counts (M3a 6, M3b 4, M3c 4, M3d 2, M3e survives, D10 16 on old rows, G1a/b/c 58/85/85, W-M1..W-M6) against yours (counts may differ by grouping: say so).

