## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the four; a removed or changed line other than the three `sections.ts` lines and the one floor number; any byte under `src`, `docs`, `.github`, `web/src/api`, `OnePager.tsx`, `ProposalDocument.tsx`, fixtures, CSS, a project file; **any user-facing string other than `All device classes` changed or added**; **the rendered device-class cell of a deal-wide row not exactly `All device classes` in the one-pager OR in the full proposal**; a skip, `.only`-style gate, environment gate or sleep in an added row; a lost test name; a non-ASCII byte, ticket key, finding or mutant id, card id, percent figure or person's name in an added line or message; a secret; **a build warning, a failed or skipped test on the head tree or the combined tree, a merge conflict between the head and main, or any PR check-run failed or cancelled**; a new open alert; the head moved; a new row red at the head. *Major:* **B566-1 not closed: M3a, M3b or M3c survives, or is killed only by an old row, or M3a stays green on the whole Api project**; **a near-miss spelling (W2-W5) or a null-branch mutant (W6, W7, W10) of the words survives the web suite**; the constant reaches a place the product owner's ruling does not name and prints the words there (the summary table, a stream label, a section row, the Media row); a differential disagreement at the head (or no power under W1, W2, W6); a non-equivalent survivor you cannot prove equivalent that sits at or above 0.01 page; a new row that no mutant turns red; a builder claim contradicted (6 + 1 names, Api 2,234, web 1,273, the floor counter above 100 on both hosts, the Theory's 6/4/4/2); a repeat red; an old killer that no longer dies (D10's 16 rows). *Minor/Note:* the threshold bound (a survivor strictly inside (0, 0.01), graded by reachability as Check 4 says); **B566-6 not closed** (the floor line is `>= 100` but G1 does not turn it red, or the counter at the head is not above 100 on both hosts: Minor, as round 1 graded it); the floor line's counter now counts per deal (a Note); the longer cell's fit (NOT TESTED, a Note); the old comment's "summary table" claim (gone, a Note only if still present anywhere); the round-1 Notes not built (B566-3, -4, -5, -7); CI timing; the timing-sensitive Api test passing on rerun. If a closure that round 1 graded Minor stays open, grade it Minor again; if one graded Major stays open, it is Major. Do not soften a Major to avoid the cap; do not harden a Minor to force it.
**ROUND-CAP STATEMENT (binding; copy it into your STATUS verdict section).** This is **round 2 of 2, the cap.** For EVERY finding say whether it is a closed instance of the round-1 class (B566-1 .. B566-7) or a new one. A GO or GO WITH FINDINGS lets Tuesday land #105 once the checks are green (landing rule under Check 7). **A NO GO does not start a round 3: the closed instances stay closed (nothing is reverted; the PR keeps what you proved), the rest is ticketed, and a third round needs the product owner's word** (Tuesday writes the card).

**First line of STATUS:** `GATE VERDICT B581: #105 b561 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ ce6aedf (round 2 of 2 - THE CAP - delta <3 commits, 4 paths, +47 -4 y/n; src/docs/.github/api bytes 0 y/n; removed lines exactly the 3 sections.ts lines and the floor number y/n; names lost n added n> - closure <B566-1 y/n, B566-6 y/n> - words <the cell reads exactly All device classes in the one-pager y/n and in the full proposal y/n; constant reaches only the two named tables y/n; other user-facing literals changed n> - rows <web it red at 4db8661d y/n, green at the head y/n; Theory green at the head y/n; each new row killed by a named mutant y/n> - mutants <server killed n of m; M3a M3b M3c M3d killed n of 4 by new rows only y/n; bound survivors <names|none>; web killed n of m; W2-W5 killed y/n; G1 turns >= 100 red and >= 20 green y/n; controls c0 c1 c2 c3 cw-weak as expected y/n> - differential <seed 581101, n variants, disagreements n, power W1 n W2 n W6 n> - CI line head tree <Engine n, Import n, Api n, web n files n tests, warnings n, failed n> and combined tree <Engine n, Import n, Api n, conflicts n, warnings n, failed n> - checks <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CodeQL <open alerts n, analyses n of 4> - merge <mergeable, mergeable_state, 3 ahead 0 behind y/n; merge ref <sha7> stale y/n> - lanes sharing a path <n>, #102 shared <n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict, incl. the merge ref and its parents), instrument and load, your predictions (written first), checks 1-9 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B581-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, closed-instance or new, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the mutant table and the row-kill table, the rendered-cell table (document, fixture, cell text, code points), the check-run table with the PENDING set per poll, the ROUND-CAP STATEMENT, FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; whether #105 can land now and the landing line; the tier call confirmed or "tier 1 recommended"; "the PR #105 checks are <state>"), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports, slots and trees left, **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly:** `VERDICT: B581 #105 b561/mps-proposal-combined-usage-rate @ ce6aedf <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round 2 of 2, the cap; PR #105 open; CI <complete|pending: names>) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.
